        "prompt": "$(y^3)^4\\div y^{\\boxed{\\rule{0pt}{3mm}\\hspace{3mm}}}=y^7$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "5",
          "worked": "$(y^3)^4=y^{12}$. Division subtracts the indices, so $12-\\square=7$ and $\\square=5$. Check: $y^{12}\\div y^5=y^7$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-x-topic-3-practice-slot-4-slot-4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(k^{\\boxed{\\rule{0pt}{3mm}\\hspace{3mm}}})^2\\times k^3=k^{11}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "4",
          "worked": "$k^3$ is multiplied, so the power of a power has index $11-3=8$. Since $\\square\\times2=8$, $\\square=4$. Check: $(k^4)^2\\times k^3=k^8\\times k^3=k^{11}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
